lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in:\n  - v4.8.dev5.mono.official [9552dfb68]\n  - v4.8.dev6.mono.official [8898c2b3d]\n- Not reproducible in: \n  - v4.7.2.stable.mono.official [ed1daf0bf]\n  - v4.8.dev4.mono.official [b56a91878]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev6.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Single-window, 1 monitor (2560x1440 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-9900 CPU @ 3.10GHz (16 threads) - 31.93 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSince 4.8.dev5, when setting a `GPUParticles3D`s \"Transform Align\" property to \"Billboard\", the particles ignore everything thats configured in the scale of the `ParticleProcessMaterial` (Scale, Scale Curve, Scale 3D).\nIt does not make a difference whether the Mesh material uses its \"Billboard\" or \"Keep Scale\" settings.\n\n| dev4 | dev6 |\n|------|------|\n|<img width=\"169\" height=\"362\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a725a49-b94b-4b0a-aa9a-e8a2b1dc6c83\" /> |<img width=\"191\" height=\"344\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5335d96f-93c7-43b0-a753-4d05429313f8\" /> |\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a GPUParticles3D Node\n- Configure a ParticleProcessMaterial with Scale settings\n- Set the \"Transform Align\" property to \"Billboard\" on the GPUParticles3D Node\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nWhile the reproduction steps are not project dependent, you can find the project I used for testing and screenshots here:\n[bug-particle-scale-MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32375747/bug-particle-scale-MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"